# NetApp GSD Recipe context

Read before changing the recipe, install workflow, or target-repo behavior:

1. **Recipe commands:** [docs/RECIPE-COMMANDS.md](docs/RECIPE-COMMANDS.md) — full catalog; invoke **`recipe-help`** in Cursor for a guided tour.
2. **Native GSD commands:** invoke **`gsd-help`** in Cursor (bundled GSD skills under `.cursor/skills/gsd-*`).
3. **Recipe policy:** [docs/netapp-recipe/lld/PLANNING-POLICY.md](docs/netapp-recipe/lld/PLANNING-POLICY.md) — mandatory PLAN.md sections and per-phase prerequisites.
4. **Install LLD:** [docs/netapp-recipe/lld/INSTALL-LLD.md](docs/netapp-recipe/lld/INSTALL-LLD.md) — scaffold, verify, uninstall.
5. **Backlog:** [docs/netapp-recipe/BACKLOG.md](docs/netapp-recipe/BACKLOG.md) — task status and dependencies.
6. **Roadmap:** [.planning/ROADMAP.md](.planning/ROADMAP.md) — project phases (when present in target repos).

Install into a target repo: `bench/runners/install-recipe-to-target.sh --target /path/to/repo`

Regenerate command docs after catalog changes: `bench/lib/generate-recipe-help.sh`

**Never invoke GSD skills** (`gsd-new-project`, `gsd-plan-phase`, etc.) on behalf of the user unless they explicitly asked you to run a recipe wrapper skill that documents same-turn native calls.

When a native GSD workflow suggests a `gsd-*` command as the operator's next action, translate it using `.cursor/rules/recipe-command-surface.mdc`.
